  "goodToKnow": "Der Erzbischof is an archbishop, the head of an Erzbistum (archdiocese) such as Köln, München und Freising or Salzburg. The prefix Erz- means arch- and also appears in der Erzfeind (arch-enemy) and der Erzengel (archangel). Germany has seven Erzbistümer. The Cologne cathedral, Kölner Dom, is the seat of the Archbishop of Cologne. Das Erz, by itself, means ore."
